der-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-8" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:StandardProductWarrantyAccrualNoncurrent" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="3" id="f-592">18,066</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/><td colspan="3" style="display:none"/></tr></table></div></ix:nonNumeric><div style="margin-top:9pt;text-indent:36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The most significant component of our warranty liability was in the North America segment. As of June 27, 2026, the warranty liability in the North America segment totaled $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-104" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:StandardProductWarrantyAccrual" scale="6" id="f-593">34.6</ix:nonFraction> million, after discounting future estimated cash flows at rates between <ix:nonFraction unitRef="number" contextRef="c-105" decimals="4" name="us-gaap:ProductLiabilityContingencyAccrualDiscountRate" scale="-2" id="f-594">3.90</ix:nonFraction>% and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="number" contextRef="c-106" decimals="4" name="us-gaap:ProductLiabilityContingencyAccrualDiscountRate" scale="-2" id="f-595">4.39</ix:nonFraction>%. Without discounting, the liability would have increased by approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-6" decimals="-5" name="jeld:StandardProductWarrantyAccrualDiscountAdjustment" scale="6" id="f-596">2.8</ix:nonFraction> million.</span></div></ix:continuation><div style="height:36pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="margin-top:9pt;text-align:center;text-indent:36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">F-18</span></div></div></div><div id="i9be55db4afc84d05962177e377352c1a_142"></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:36pt;width:100%"><div style="margin-top:9pt"><span style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline"><a style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline" href="#i9be55db4afc84d05962177e377352c1a_7">Back to top</a></span></div></div><div style="margin-top:12pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Note 10. <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-1" name="us-gaap:DebtDisclosureTextBlock" id="f-597" continuedAt="f-597-1" escape="true">Long-Term Debt</ix:nonNumeric></span></div><ix:continuation id="f-597-1" continuedAt="f-597-2"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-1" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfDebtInstrumentsTextBlock" id="f-598" continuedAt="f-598-1" escape="true"><div style="margin-top:9pt;text-indent:36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Our long-term debt, net of unamortized debt issuance costs and original issue discounts, consisted of the following:</span></div><div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:center"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:30.983%"/><t